--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Protocol §3.10 reporting rule -- apply when writing these up:
  * zero treated support or non-computable bootstrap -> "not estimable"
  * attrition diagnostic p_WCB < 0.05 -> report balanced-composition and IPSW estimates alongside the unbalanced headline, state |delta_beta|, and describe the magnitude as NOT POINT-IDENTIFIED under differential attrition
  * agree in sign, small |delta_beta| -> "direction identified; magnitude sensitive to composition"; disagree in sign -> "sign not identified"
  * underpowered == 1 (fewer than 3 treated clusters) -> report as underpowered, NEVER as a null result
  * an interval containing zero never supports a direction
  * phase:* rows are the 2026-09-13 robustness arm, exposure classified against each district's BASELINE markers; the frozen headline:* rows remain the headline
  * pretrend rows (§3.9): a lead coefficient distinguishable from zero invalidates parallel trends for that exposure class; the corresponding headline coefficient is then not causal
